  "author": "PingYou Ltd",
  "kind": "new finite construction",
  "attribution_note": "Original source packing by Timo Berthold, Dominik Kamp, Gioni Mexi, Sebastian Pokutta and Imre P\u00f3lik. Original credit: Published construction by Timo Berthold, Dominik Kamp, Gioni Mexi, Sebastian Pokutta and Imre P\u00f3lik; imported and checked without transferring discovery credit.. Classical Cartesian partitions are used. PingYou Ltd supplies this finite mixed assembly and native certificate. PingYou Ltd supplies the subsequent coupled whole-block translation return.",
  "construction": {
   "name": "joint_complete_block_translation_return",
   "proof": "Complete source-block translation return\n\nStart with each of the twelve reviewed complete native mixed-box controls.\nThe block label is the first entry of its retained [block, source-owner] word.\nFor every block z introduce ONE vector u_z. Every owner a in that block has\ncenter c_a+u_z and keeps its original quaternion. Thus its actual internal\ngeometry is fixed throughout the ideal return. Remove the containing-box\nwalls from the optimization: those were sufficient construction devices,\nnot physical walls between the owners.\n\nFor each actual cross-block pair a,b retain a rational separating normal n\ncertified at the source control. Compute g_ab as an exact outward lower\nbound for min(n.X_b)-max(n.X_a) from their complete native vertices. Impose\nn.u_a-n.u_b <= g_ab. This is ONE simultaneous linear system over all blocks;\nseparately feasible pair motions are never combined. Each real host wall\nhas its own complete-owner support h_a: sign*u_z[k]-S/2 <= -h_a.\nMinimize the ONE host side S. No frame/angle variable exists.\n\nThe original u=0,S=S_source is a strict feasible control. The numerical LP\nendpoint is only a proposal. Rationalize its full shared variable vector,\nthen mix it with the original state using ONE exact lambda determined by\nevery retained wall/pair row. This restores strict shared compatibility\nwithout dilating or changing internal block geometry. Every point along\nthe resulting segment satisfies the same rows by convexity. Retain the\nuncontracted source, full rows, controller labels, endpoint and lambda.\nThe final binary64 centers and outward side are checked again natively;\ntheir tiny coordinate rounding is distinct from the exact translation law.\n\nCompare all twelve full controls to fresh complete public/private thresholds\nfirst. Only then retain those literal prefixes for which the complete\ntranslated control itself predicts a strict threshold crossing; do not\nrun a blind prefix optimization sweep. A later deleted-controller return\nwould be a separately derived operation.\n\nThe sources contain seven complete m-owner donors and one complete M-owner donor in eight distinct cubical cells. Their common original host side is a+b. The source intervals were already proved mutually compatible. The present return removes only those internal artificial cells; it does not delete any source owner or alter any inherited frame. Source controls and all resulting neutral or failed threshold cases remain retained.\n",
