     "attribution_note": "Original source packing by Timo Berthold, Dominik Kamp, Gioni Mexi, Sebastian Pokutta and Imre P\u00f3lik. Original credit: Published construction by Timo Berthold, Dominik Kamp, Gioni Mexi, Sebastian Pokutta and Imre P\u00f3lik; imported and checked without transferring discovery credit.. Classical Cartesian partitions are used. PingYou Ltd supplies this finite mixed assembly and native certificate.",
     "construction": {
      "name": "seven_small_one_large_complete_block_composition",
      "proof": "Mixed complete-block composition.\n\nLet a complete m-owner packing lie in a cube of side a, and a complete\nM-owner packing of the same canonical solid lie in a cube of side b>=a.\nSubtract each source cube center from its actual owner centers. For every\nsign word sigma in {-1,1}^3 except (1,1,1), place one complete small source\nat cube center sigma*a/2. Place one complete large source at (b/2,b/2,b/2).\nThe eight containing cubes have disjoint interiors, separated by actual\ncoordinate planes. Their union lies in [-a,b]^3. Subtract the ONE common\nhost center ((b-a)/2,(b-a)/2,(b-a)/2); the host side is a+b.\n\nThe full owner count is 7*m+M. All original owner frames and each donor's\ninternal geometry are retained. Between blocks, one coordinate plane\nseparates both whole containing cubes; no independently chosen marginal\nplacement occurs. Any declared smaller count is a literal complete-owner\nprefix of this same common configuration.\n\nFor a strict native certificate, multiply every resulting center by the\nsame rho=10000001/10000000, retaining unit owner size and actual quaternion.\nEvery canonical solid here has the origin strictly inside, so every\nsupport value is positive. Thus dilation of centers opens each separating\ngap and increases host margins in a cube of side rho*(a+b). Round each\nexact rational center once to binary64, and the common host side outward\nwith 1e-7 additional clearance. Check every resulting native pair and wall.\n\nThe Cartesian partition is classical. Every original donor author and\nmethod remains attached; PingYou Ltd supplies the finite mixed assembly\nand its complete native certificate. No optimum is claimed.\n",
